*coat*
!/linux/.config/coat/
!/linux/.config/coat/coat.yaml
linux/.config/coat/schemes/

# Files coat OWNS entirely (it rewrites them on every `coat set`), as opposed to
# the fragments it writes alongside a config — those already match the *coat*
# rule above. These tools have no include mechanism, so coat generates the
# whole file and tracking them would mean a dirty tree after every theme change.
# (labwc joined on 2026-08-17; note its path is a THEME dir, not .config/labwc --
# labwc ignores themerc in the config dir. See coat's apply_labwc.)
# The templates that produce them live in ~/Projects/coat/templates/.
linux/.config/fnott/fnott.ini
linux/.config/swaylock/config
linux/.local/share/themes/coat/labwc/themerc
# ...and the traffic-light buttons coat renders next to it. Note stow FOLDS
# ~/.local/share/themes/coat into a symlink straight at this package directory, so
# coat writes these into the repo, not into a separate target tree. The .xbm files in
# that directory are hand-made and ARE tracked -- they are the fallback for a labwc
# built without librsvg, and unlike svg they are masks that labwc recolours itself.
linux/.local/share/themes/coat/labwc/*.svg
linux/.config/wob/wob.ini

# py_compile droppings — the scripts in .local/bin are run directly, never imported.
__pycache__/
*.pyc
